# Theme & Palette Rules

Based on [VS Code Color Theme API](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/color-theme): workbench `colors` + TextMate `tokenColors`. Ether derives both from palette tokens — never patch generated theme JSON.

## Current palettes (25 dark)

All palette sources live in `src/palettes/ether-{name}.js`. Examples:

| ID | Side panel (`surfacePanel`) | Editor (`surfaceEditor`) | Character |
|----|----------------------------|--------------------------|-----------|
| `ether-graphite` | `#161618` | `#1C1C1E` | Pure neutral gray |
| `ether-storm` | `#181C22` | `#1C2028` | Cool blue-gray |
| `ether-dusk` | `#1A1820` | `#1E1C28` | Plum twilight |

Run `pnpm run build:extension` after palette edits. Full list: `src/palettes/` (25 files).

All palettes are **dark only** (`type: "dark"`, `uiTheme: "vs-dark"`). Each must feel unique via surface temperature and accent — not neon or oversaturated syntax.

## Adding or editing a palette

Create/edit `src/palettes/ether-{name}.js`:

```js
export default {
  id: "ether-{name}",       // matches filename stem
  label: "Ether {Name}",
  type: "dark",
  uiTheme: "vs-dark",
  ui: { accent, fgPrimary, surfacePanel, surfaceEditor, /* … */ },
  syntax: { default, comment, string, keyword, /* role keys */ },
};
```

Copy an existing palette as a template. All `ui` and `syntax` keys are validated at build time.

### Anchor-first workflow (required)

**Do not** pick accent or syntax colors first. Build surfaces in this order:

1. **Anchors** — set `surfacePanel` (sidebar) and `surfaceEditor` (editor). Panel is slightly darker than editor; both share the same hue family.
2. **Surface stack** — derive darker/lighter steps from the anchors:
   - `surfaceBorder` → darkest chrome edge
   - `surfaceShell` → below panel
   - `surfacePanel` → sidebar, tabs inactive, status bar (anchor)
   - `surfaceEditor` → editor + composer pane (anchor)
   - `surfaceLineHighlight` → current line, one step above editor
   - `surfaceInput`, `surfaceHover`, `surfaceWidget`, `surfaceNotification`, `surfaceListFocus` — interpolate between panel and editor or one step lighter
   - `surfacePeek` → usually matches `surfaceShell`
3. **Foreground** — `fgPrimary` (7:1 on editor), `fgMuted` / `fgActivity` (4.5:1 on editor), `fgListFocus`, `fgOnAccent` (4.5:1 on accent).
4. **Accent** — one muted hue aligned with the surface family (steel blue on cool grays, copper on warm, sage on green, etc.).
5. **Syntax** — restrained role colors that harmonize with the surface temperature; verify all 10 palette syntax roles pass contrast on `surfaceEditor`. Comment color is derived at build from `fgMuted` (do not author `syntax.comment` in palettes).
6. **Terminal & git** — match the palette family; reuse accent/modified/added/deleted patterns from a sibling palette if unsure.

Example anchor pairs already in the catalog:

```
Graphite:  panel #161618  →  editor #1C1C1E   (neutral)
Storm:     panel #181C22  →  editor #1C2028   (cool blue-gray)
```

Workbench mapping: `sideBar.background` = `surfacePanel`, `editor.background` = `surfaceEditor`, composer/agent inputs = `surfaceEditor` (see `derive-extensions.js`).

## Workbench derivation (required path)

1. **New workbench key** → add to `src/workbench/core-catalog.js` OR `extension-catalog.js`.
2. **Derive the value** in `derive-core.js` (core) or `derive-extensions.js` (menus, tabs, etc.).
3. Keys in `TRANSPARENT_WORKBENCH_COLOR_IDS` must use alpha via `withAlphaByte` (not opaque `#RRGGBB`).

Use `mixColors`, `withAlphaByte`, `darken` from `src/utils/color.js` — not ad-hoc hex math.

### Interactive states (hover / selection)

Shared logic lives in `src/workbench/derive-interactive.js`. **Never** pair accent-tinted hover backgrounds with `fgMuted` text — contrast collapses (status bar bug).

| Pattern | Background | Foreground |
|---------|------------|------------|
| List hover / selection / focus | `surfaceListFocus` | `fgListFocus` |
| List inactive selection | `surfaceHover` | accent |
| Neutral overlay (status bar, secondary buttons) | `fgPrimary` at 15–30% alpha | `fgPrimary` → `fgListFocus` on hover |
| Tabs / menus / quick pick focus | `surfaceListFocus` | `fgListFocus` |
| Activity bar active icon | — | `fgPrimary` + `activeBorder` accent |
| Suggest widget selected row | `surfaceListFocus` | `fgListFocus` |
| Primary / prominent buttons | solid accent | `fgOnButton`; hover uses `accentHover` |

List rows sit on `surfacePanel` — do **not** set `list.hoverBackground` to `surfacePanel` (invisible hover).

## Syntax highlighting

- Rules live in `src/syntax/rules.js` — one shared set across all themes (currently 58 rules).
- Map scopes to `syntax.{role}` tokens: `default`, `string`, `number`, `cyan`, `keyword`, `variable`, `function`, `type`, `red`, `pink` (plus derived `comment` at build).
- `SYNTAX_RULE_COUNT` must equal `EXPECTED_SYNTAX_RULE_COUNT`; tests enforce this.
- Enable `semanticHighlighting: true` in generated themes (scope-map fallback; no hand-authored `semanticTokenColors`).
- **Do not** add `semanticTokenColors` or `settings.background` on token rules.
- **Italic policy**: comments, doc comments, keywords, decorators, inherited classes, CSS `@`-rules — yes. Functions, types, tags, identifiers, parameters — no.

## Contrast & validation

Build fails if palette tokens miss WCAG targets in `PALETTE_CONTRAST_TARGETS`:

| Token | Minimum ratio (on `surfaceEditor` unless noted) |
|-------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `ui.fgPrimary` | 7:1 |
| `syntax.default` | 7:1 |
| `ui.fgMuted`, all other `syntax.*` | 4.5:1 |
| `ui.fgOnAccent` | 4.5:1 (on `ui.accent`) |

Tune base tokens in `src/palettes/` — there is no post-build syntax tuning script. Comments on darker editors (e.g. `#161E2A`, `#181E2C`) often need to be brighter than on neutral grays.

## Removing a theme

Delete the palette file and run `pnpm run build` — orphaned JSON and `package.json` entries are cleaned automatically.
